---
Configurable Randomize panel for drum patterns + synths.

Today the RND button (TASK-223) only randomizes sampler step
velocities using built-in style probabilities. The user wants
finer control over what gets rolled.

## Proposed UI
A compact popover anchored to the RND toolbar button (or a
right-click on it) with checkboxes:

  [x] Randomize pattern steps      (velocity on/off per step)
  [ ] Randomize kit                (cycle sq_kits[] or, once
                                    TASK-224 lands, draw from the
                                    auto-imported pool)
  [ ] Randomize synth notes        (piano-roll notes for the
                                    trap-808 / pad tracks, within
                                    a user-selectable key + octave)
  [ ] Randomize velocity spread    (re-roll velocities on existing
                                    hits within a min/max range —
                                    matches the right-click-drag
                                    pad editor's velocity scope)
  [ ] Randomize micro-timing       (adds per-step micro_offset
                                    for humanize feel)
  [ ] Randomize pitch offsets      (per-step pitch_offset, matches
                                    the right-click-drag pad
                                    editor's pitch scope)

  Style: [four-on-floor / boom-bap / trap / breakbeat / any]
  Seed:  [optional, blank = random]
  [Apply] button.

Style dropdown lets the user bias the result; the engine already
has style-specific profiles in random_pattern.c that we can wire
up to this selection.

## Engine changes
- Extend sq_pattern_randomize() to take an options struct:
    typedef struct {
        bool steps, velocity, micro, pitch, notes;
        int  style;   /* -1 = random, 0..3 = specific style */
        int  seed;    /* 0 = time-based */
    } sq_random_options_t;
- Add per-flag helper functions (randomize_velocity, randomize_pitch,
  randomize_notes) that operate on an existing pattern in-place.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Right-click (or dedicated popover) on RND opens the settings
- [ ] Each checkbox toggles its category independently
- [ ] Style dropdown changes the distribution bias
- [ ] Ctrl+R uses the last-applied settings
- [ ] Settings persisted in the app state (session.json)
- [ ] Undoable (single undo_push before applying)
- [ ] Frontend parity (ImGui + GTK)

## Test Plan
- [ ] Apply with only "velocity" checked → existing steps get new
      velocities, pattern structure unchanged
- [ ] Apply with only "notes" checked → synth tracks get new notes,
      sampler tracks unchanged
- [ ] Apply with "kit" checked → kit index changes + samples reload
